part soc_6
  tally 1
  law
  note "SOC-6 · Indexation: on 1 March each year every pension that started before 1 March of the year before is multiplied by PEN-IDX-<yyyy>; one that started later from the first 1 March after a full year of payment (.1); rounded, a top-up recomputed and not indexed (.2)."
  note "PEN-IDX-<yyyy> rows govern the year of the indexation they are for (GEN-6)."

source soc_6 "Social Insurance Act, SOC-6 Indexation of pensions (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

index soc6_year = year 2018..2064

input pen_idx[y in soc6_year]: num question "By what factor are pensions multiplied on 1 March of this year (PEN-IDX, SOC-6 .1)?"

